---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Passage = `THE LOYALTY CARD

A grocery chain gives shoppers a discount if they scan a loyalty
card at the till. Scanning records what was bought, at which
store, and at what time, against the shopper's account.

An account is created with a name, a date of birth, and either a
phone number or an email address. The chain says it needs the
date of birth because some products cannot be sold to minors.

There is also an app. Shoppers who install it get extra offers.
The app reports the phone's location while it is running, and the
chain uses that to send an offer when a shopper is near a store.

Coupons are chosen by a program that looks at what an account has
bought before. A shopper complained after receiving coupons for
products she had not bought and had told no one she needed. The
chain said the program had found that accounts buying the same
combination of items she had bought often went on to buy those
products.

Purchase summaries are sold to the companies that make the
products. The names are removed first, and those companies do not
receive account details.

The chain's terms say an account can be closed at any time.
Closing an account stops new records being added. The chain keeps
the records it already holds for seven years, which it says is
required for tax purposes.

The discount is only available with a card.`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Question Set 19: Reading Passage</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">
          Five questions &middot; one passage &middot; 12 minutes
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Is</h2>

          <p>
            <b>Due session 60, while you are building.</b> No code, nothing to
            run, nothing to install.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>The second reading passage of this quarter, and it is about data
            collection rather than effects.</b> Question Set 17 asked what a
            program <i>did</i> to people. This one asks what a program{" "}
            <i>knows</i> about them, and how it came to know it.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>You have not been taught this content yet either.</b> Everything
            the questions ask about is in the passage. Part 3 covers it properly
            at Activity 3.16.
          </p>

          <h4>How to Do This One</h4>

          <ul>
            <li>
              <b>Read the whole passage first.</b> The detail that matters most
              is usually not in the paragraph the question points at.
            </li>
            <li><b>Set a timer for 12 minutes.</b> The reading is part of it.</li>
            <li>
              <b>Every answer is in the passage or follows from it.</b> You do
              not need to know anything about how real supermarkets work, and
              what you already believe about them is not evidence.
            </li>
            <li>Mark each answer <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>, as always.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="passage">
          <h2>The Passage</h2>

          <Code
            code={Passage}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="Read this before looking at the questions"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="questions">
          <h2>The Questions</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 1</h3>

          <p>
            The shopper received coupons for products she had not bought and had
            told no one she needed. Based on the passage, how did the program
            reach that result?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) The chain read her messages or her search history</li>
            <li>(B) The program made a random guess that happened to be correct</li>
            <li>(C) Ordinary purchases were combined with the patterns of other accounts to infer something she had not disclosed</li>
            <li>(D) An employee at the chain recognized her and chose the coupons</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 2 &mdash; Select all that apply</h3>

          <p>
            Which of these does the passage say the chain holds, that could
            identify or describe an individual shopper?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) A name</li>
            <li>(B) A date of birth</li>
            <li>(C) A phone number or an email address</li>
            <li>(D) The phone's location while the app is running</li>
            <li>(E) The names of the companies that make the products</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 3</h3>

          <p>
            A shopper closes her account. Which statement is best supported by
            the passage?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) Every record of her purchases is removed</li>
            <li>(B) Her records are sold to the manufacturers when the account closes</li>
            <li>(C) The chain has to delete the records as soon as she asks</li>
            <li>(D) No new records are added, and the records already held remain for seven years</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 4</h3>

          <p>
            The chain says it collects a date of birth because some products
            cannot be sold to minors. What is the <b>strongest</b> objection to
            collecting it when the account is created?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) A date of birth cannot identify anybody, so collecting it achieves nothing</li>
            <li>(B) The restriction applies at the till and to particular products, so a date of birth on every account is not what enforces it</li>
            <li>(C) The chain has no legitimate reason to know a shopper's age under any circumstances</li>
            <li>(D) Shoppers would enter a false date anyway, so the data is worthless</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 5</h3>

          <p>
            The discount is only available with a card. Which effect does this
            most directly create?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) Shoppers who do not want their purchases recorded pay more for the same goods</li>
            <li>(B) The chain collects less data than it otherwise would</li>
            <li>(C) The app becomes mandatory for every shopper</li>
            <li>(D) Purchase summaries can no longer be sold to manufacturers</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Five answers, each marked <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>, plus how far
            you got when the timer went off. Worth <b>5 points</b>, graded on
            completion.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>And one written answer, in a sentence or two:</b> the passage says
            purchase summaries are sold with the names removed. Say what a
            manufacturer could still learn from them, using only what the passage
            tells you.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Start the Timer
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
